    "searchCoverage": "Official Browser Use Cloud API v3 at https://api.browser-use.com/api/v3 with X-Browser-Use-API-Key. GET /billing/account is the cheap authenticated billing probe used by the pinned validator. GET /sessions and GET /sessions/{id} are reads. POST /sessions is billed and omitted. Native pins v3 only; v4 proxy routing is not expressed. Dated 2026-09-13 incident search recorded the March 2026 litellm CLI supply-chain and patched CVE-2025-47241; no current unresolved Cloud API-key compromise is asserted.",
    "incidents": [
      {
        "incidentDate": "2026-03-24",
        "disclosureDate": "2026-03-24",
        "affectedProduct": "browser-use CLI install.sh / litellm PyPI dependency",
        "affectedData": "Reported local credential harvest from machines that installed the CLI during the malicious litellm window; not documented as api.browser-use.com customer API keys.",
        "status": "confirmed historical OSS CLI supply-chain incident",
        "source": "https://github.com/browser-use/browser-use/issues/4505",
        "remediation": "PyPI removed malicious litellm versions; Browser Use dropped litellm from core dependencies and published cleanup steps.",
        "residualRisk": "Historical CLI-install residual; live Cloud API authentication unverified."
      }
